            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0472" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/392½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">10 May, 1915</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: This needs no comment
                    now, since the whole suspicious business has lost for the time being its
                    critical character.</p>
                <p>I think that Sir Edward Grey acted very well and very wisely in the matter, and I
                    believe that your personal message to Count Okuma will have more than a
                    temporary effect on his mind.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
